findings.detail:
`pgvectorChecked` is a module-level singleton (line 34) set on first call and never re-evaluated. `resetPgvectorCache()` at line 45 is documented as a test seam and has no production caller.

The worker (`pnpm worker`, src/server/jobs/worker.ts) is a long-lived process. If it boots against a database where the extension is not yet present — a fresh environment, a rolling deploy where the app starts before the migration lands, a restore from a dump taken before the extension was added — the `false` sticks for the process lifetime:

- every `persist()` call takes the line 249 branch and stores text only, leaving `embedded_at` NULL forever;
- every `recordRun` writes `vector_stage_ran = false` with the note at engine.ts:500-501 blaming a missing extension that is in fact present;
- `pendingEmbeddings` (line 277) — the input the backfill is supposed to read — also reports `vectorAvailable: false` and switches to the `embedded_text is null` predicate, so rows that already have text but no vector are not listed as pending and the backfill silently finds nothing to do.

The only recovery is a full process restart, and nothing on any screen or in any log says that is what's needed. Cache with a TTL, or key it to a value that changes when the schema does.

