Make an unsubscribe facility impossible to omit, by folding channel into a discriminated union so a mismatched or missing facility fails to compile.

In src/server/outbound/gate.ts, replace the channel + optional-bag signature (lines 134-152):

  export type UnsubscribeFacility =
    | { channel: "email"; url: string }
    | { channel: "sms"; keyword: string };

  export function withComplianceFooter(
    body: string,
    agency: { name: string; licence: string | null },
    unsubscribe: UnsubscribeFacility,
  ): string {
    if (unsubscribe.channel === "sms") {
      return `${body.trim()}\n${agency.name}. Reply ${unsubscribe.keyword} to opt out.`;
    }
    return [
      body.trim(),
      "",
      "—",
      agency.licence ? `${agency.name} · ${agency.licence}` : agency.name,
      `Unsubscribe: ${unsubscribe.url}`,   // unconditional — no `if`
    ].join("\n");
  }

Dropping the separate `channel` parameter is the load-bearing half: it removes the state where channel is "email" and the facility is an SMS keyword, which is the exact shape of the current bug. Removing `?` from `url` and `keyword` without unifying them would still allow `{}`.

send.ts:45 then fails to compile for the email branch, which is the intended forcing function. Resolve it by moving the composition inside each branch of sendMessage (send.ts:49-55) so SMS keeps working and email refuses explicitly, mirroring the alphanumeric-sender guard at send.ts:95-101:

