Cover it with two tests in tests/outbound.test.ts, using the existing grantConsent helper: (a) sms revoked 90 days ago, sms granted 30 days ago, do_not_contact false, then POST a 302 delivery report for the item's provider_message_id — expect a new revoked row to exist with occurredAt after the grant, checkConsent(..., "sms") to return allowed:false, and contacts.do_not_contact to be true; (b) sms already revoked as the latest row, POST the 302 twice — expect exactly one revocation row (no stacking) and do_not_contact still true.

