Two supporting changes, both cheap:

1. Align the schema cap with the prompt. Either state the cap explicitly in prompts/rank-matches.v1.md's Output section ("Return at most 30 matches") or drop `.max(30)` (engine.ts:77) — as written the constraint is enforced only by zod, and violating it destroys the match_runs row rather than degrading. Stating it in the prompt is the better half of the pair since the "fewer, better matches" guidance already points that way.

2. Make the loss of the run observable. runTask throwing before recordRun means a failed stage 3 leaves no match_runs row at all, which contradicts the file's own stated purpose. Wrap the runTask call in try/catch and recordRun with stage3: 0 and a note (the match_runs table already has a `note text` column, drizzle/0010_embeddings.sql) before rethrowing, so the ops view shows an attempted run that failed rather than silence.

